This plugin contains no code or text copied from other projects. Several of its design ideas come
from these projects, credited with thanks:

- anthropics/claude-plugins-official (code-review): parallel review lenses, an eligibility check,
  and the list of findings that reviews should leave out.
- addyosmani/adverse: review lenses that stay in their lane, a challenge round, provenance labels
  and its published lessons on failure modes.
- ng/adversarial-review: mechanical checks before model calls, evidence-tied confidence, and
  labeling instead of silently dropping.
- poteto/noodle: scaling the number of review lenses with the size of the change.
- basicmachines-co/basic-memory: mutual refutation and confidence derived from provenance.
- "Adversarial Review: Structured Disagreement for Grounded Agentic Code Review" (Qiu and Gill,
  2026): requiring evidence for a refutation.
